1. Definitions

1.1. "Licensor" means each copyright holder that owns rights in a portion of
the Software and has authority to offer that portion under this License.

1.2. "You" or "Recipient" means the individual or legal entity exercising
rights under this License.

1.3. "Software" means the source code, assets, build files, and official
binary forms in the Vanylith project that are owned by a Licensor and offered
under this License. Software does not include a Third-Party Component merely
because that component is stored in the same repository, used to build the
Software, linked with the Software, or included in a distribution.

1.4. "Source Code" means the human-readable form of the Software that is
preferred for understanding and making modifications.

1.5. "Modified Version" means a version of the Software produced by modifying,
extending, replacing, deleting, or adding to Vanylith code or other material
covered by this License. A separate program that merely communicates with
Vanylith through ordinary documented interfaces, IPC, HTTP, or other normal
inter-process mechanisms, without incorporating or modifying the Software, is
not a Modified Version solely because of that communication.

1.6. "Distribution" means providing a copy of the Software or a Modified
Version, in source or binary form, to any person or entity outside Your
Internal Use group, whether publicly or to selected recipients. Distribution
includes providing a ZIP file, installer, executable, package, fork, download,
or other copy. Access permitted as Internal Use under Section 3 is not
Distribution.

1.7. "Internal Use" means use by an individual for that individual's own
purposes, or use by a company, school, laboratory, team, or other organization
for its own internal purposes. An organization may permit its employees,
officers, directors, contractors, and consultants to access and use the
Software solely on its behalf and for those internal purposes. Each contractor
or consultant must be subject to reasonable confidentiality, contractual, or
similar obligations and receives no independent right, from that access, to
use the Software for other clients or to distribute or commercialize it. Bona
fide payment for that employee's, contractor's, or consultant's work does not
remove the work from Internal Use when all of these conditions are met and the
Software or Modified Version is not distributed outside the organization and
its Internal Use group.

1.8. "Hosted Service" means a website, API, bot, server, remote interface,
managed system, network service, or similar arrangement through which an
external third party can directly use the Software, or the core vanity-address-
generation functionality implemented by or derived from the Software, without
necessarily receiving a copy of its source code or binary.

1.9. "Consideration" means direct or indirect economic value connected in
substance to the relevant software, service, functionality, result, access, or
traffic. It includes money, fiat currency, cryptocurrency, a subscription or
membership fee, credits, points, tokens, prepaid balance, a required purchase,
a bundle purchase, paid-group access, payment for access, download, entitlement,
quota, or priority, and advertising revenue, affiliate revenue, paid sponsor or
promotional placement, revenue sharing, referral commissions, or other
commercial traffic monetization materially connected to a Hosted Service or
its use. The label placed on a charge does not control. A voluntary,
unconditional Donation under Section 10 is not Consideration when it provides
no access or usage benefit and does not purchase Hosted Service traffic,
advertising, promotion, placement, or referral rights.

1.10. "Commercial Distribution" means Distribution of the Software or a
Modified Version where providing, obtaining, or accessing the copy or any
associated download, update, feature, source, binary, package, or entitlement
is directly or indirectly conditioned on Consideration. Section 8 governs bona
fide independent services.

1.11. "Commercial Hosted Service" means a Hosted Service that provides the
Software or its core vanity-address-generation functionality to external third
parties and is directly or indirectly monetized through Consideration
materially connected to the Hosted Service or its use or traffic, whether or
not users themselves are charged. It includes paid or subscription SaaS, paid
APIs or bots, pay-per-use services, purchased credits, points or tokens,
generation-for-hire, managed vanity generation, charges based on a result,
address, compute time, GPU time, attempts, or difficulty, advertising revenue,
affiliate revenue, paid sponsor or promotional placement, revenue sharing,
referral commissions, and commercial traffic monetization. A service does not
cease to be commercial merely because a button or tier is called "free."

1.12. "Corresponding Source" means the Source Code and other source-form
material that an ordinary developer would reasonably need to understand,
modify, and rebuild the particular Modified Version. As applicable, it includes
modified and added source files, patches, build scripts, CMake configuration,
relevant build configuration, source-level modifications, and required project
files. It does not include source for an operating system, standard compiler,
system libraries, or unchanged Third-Party Components.

1.13. "Vanylith Marks" or "Official Marks" means the Vanylith name, official
logo, official icon, official wordmark, and other official product branding.

1.14. "Third-Party Component" means code, a library, SDK, runtime, asset, or
other material in which rights are held by someone other than the applicable
Licensor and that is subject to separate license terms.

1.15. "Donation" means a voluntary and unconditional donation, tip, or
sponsorship that is not required to obtain or use any software, source, binary,
download, update, feature, result, priority, quota, special build, or hosted-
generation entitlement, and that does not purchase advertising, promotional or
sponsor placement, referrals, traffic, revenue sharing, or other commercial
rights connected to a Hosted Service. A neutral acknowledgement of support in
general project materials does not, by itself, prevent a payment from being a
Donation.

1.16. "Project Steward" means the individual or legal entity that, when the
Vanylith Contributor License Agreement 1.0 ("VCLA 1.0") first becomes effective
for Contributions, lawfully operates the GitHub account publicly identified as
@ByNovaLin and, under that public project identity, administers the official
Vanylith repository identified as https://github.com/ByNovaLin/vanylith.
Thereafter, another individual or legal entity becomes the Project Steward only
through a permitted assignment to a Successor Steward under Section 7 of VCLA
1.0. Mere control, sale, transfer, compromise, loss, username reassignment, or
repository technical-control change does not by itself confer Project Steward
status. The account name is a public identifier and does not represent a
separate legal entity.

