3. Internal Use and Private Modification

You may make and keep private or closed-source modifications for Your own
Internal Use. A commercial organization may use the Software and a closed-
source Modified Version internally, including in production and for its own
commercial operations, without publishing its modifications. No source-
disclosure obligation arises solely from Internal Use.

This permission does not allow Distribution of a closed-source Modified
Version or operation of a Commercial Hosted Service. Contractors and
consultants may use the Software only within the limits in Section 1.7.

4. Modification

You may create Modified Versions. You do not have to publish a Modified Version
that remains entirely within Internal Use. If You distribute a Modified
Version or use one to provide a Hosted Service, Sections 6 and 9 apply.

5. Free Redistribution of Unmodified Official Copies

You may distribute an unmodified official copy of the Software only if all of
the following conditions are met:

(a) the copy is provided without Consideration;

(b) the official files are not altered;

(c) all copyright notices, this License, NOTICE, and applicable third-party
notices are retained with the copy;

(d) You do not represent Your mirror, download, or distribution channel as an
official Vanylith site or release channel, or imply endorsement, approval,
partnership, sponsorship, affiliation, or authorization by the Licensor; and

(e) You comply with all separate terms governing Third-Party Components.

The Vanylith name, logo, icon, and wordmark already present in an unmodified
official copy may remain in that copy. This does not grant a right to use the
Vanylith Marks to brand Your own site, service, or product.

6. Distribution of Modified Versions

Except where a Licensor with sufficient authority gives separate written
permission, You may distribute a Modified Version only if all of the following
conditions are met:

(a) no Consideration is charged for the Modified Version itself, including its
license rights, source and binary forms, packages, installers, downloads,
updates, and features. This does not prohibit a bona fide independent service
fee permitted by Section 8;

(b) a usable copy of the portions of the Modified Version consisting of the
Software and modifications to the Software, together with the complete
Corresponding Source, is made freely and publicly accessible to the general
public no later than the first external Distribution of that version. A public
Git repository or unrestricted direct source archive is sufficient. Access
limited to a customer, selected recipients, or a private repository is not
sufficient. Payment, membership, paid accounts, sponsorship, private purchase,
or similar conditions for access are prohibited. The Corresponding Source must
remain publicly accessible until the later of (i) three (3) years after the
last Distribution of that version or (ii) the date You stop making that version
available;

(c) the portions of the Modified Version consisting of the Software and
modifications to the Software remain licensed under the Vanylith Community
Source License 1.0. You may not relicense those portions under MIT, a
proprietary license, a closed-source license, a commercial-only license, or
other terms that remove or reduce the requirements of this License;

(d) all applicable copyright notices, this LICENSE, NOTICE, and third-party
notices are retained;

(e) a prominent modification notice identifies the work as a modified version
or fork of Vanylith, states that it is not an official Vanylith release, and
reasonably summarizes the principal modifications; and

(f) the Modified Version uses its own name, logo, icon, and primary identity as
required by Section 14.

These requirements apply to both public and targeted external Distribution. A
targeted delivery does not comply merely because the selected recipient
receives source code; the material described in subsection (b) must also be
available to the general public. Work performed by an employee, contractor, or
consultant entirely within an organization's Internal Use under Section 1.7 is
not external Distribution and does not trigger this section. These requirements
do not require disclosure of unrelated, independently developed software that
only communicates with Vanylith through ordinary interfaces and does not
incorporate or modify the Software. Independently owned, separable components
may use separate terms, but those terms must not restrict or override the
rights and obligations applicable to the Software and its modifications.

No contributor or distributor may require a person to disclose a legal name,
government identifier, or other unnecessary private information as a condition
of obtaining a publicly offered Modified Version or its Corresponding Source.

7. No Commercial Distribution or Resale

Unless the Licensor gives separate written permission, You may not engage in
Commercial Distribution. Without limitation, You may not sell or resell the
Software or a Modified Version; charge for copies, source, binaries, installers,
packages, downloads, updates, or features; sublicense for a fee; place access
behind a subscription, membership, paid group, sponsor tier, course purchase,
or other paywall; offer a paid-only or VIP build; or include the Software as
value available only through a paid bundle or required purchase.

A charge called an installation fee, service fee, membership fee, donation,
sponsorship, course fee, or bundle price is prohibited when, in substance,
payment is required to receive the Software, a Modified Version, a download
link, source access, an update, a feature, or a license right.

8. Independent Consulting and Technical Services

You may charge for bona fide independent labor and professional services, such
as consulting, training, deployment or installation assistance, integration,
configuration, debugging, maintenance, and technical support, provided that:

(a) the customer can lawfully obtain the unmodified Software itself without
paying You;

(b) the charge is genuinely for independent labor or expertise and is not, in
substance, a condition or disguised charge for obtaining a copy, download,
license right, source access, update, feature, or special build;

(c) You do not impose proprietary or closed-source terms on the Software or on
modifications to the Software; and

(d) when an organization hires You solely to work on its behalf and for its own
Internal Use, and the conditions in Section 1.7 are met, You may create, access,
and deliver that organization's private Modified Version within its Internal
Use group without public source disclosure; and

(e) any other delivery of a Modified Version is external Distribution and must
comply with Section 6, including general-public availability of the
Vanylith-covered portions and Corresponding Source. A customer-only source
delivery is not sufficient.

Fees reasonably attributable to actual labor do not become software license
fees merely because the work involves Vanylith. However, this section cannot be
used to disguise Commercial Distribution, including withholding an otherwise
available executable or download until an "installation" fee is paid, or
charging multiple customers for delivery of a pre-existing or repeatable
Modified Version. Proprietary external delivery requires separate written
permission from a rights holder with sufficient authority.

9. Hosted Services

9.1. Free Hosted Services. You may provide a genuinely free and noncommercial
Hosted Service using an unmodified copy of the Software if users are not
required to provide Consideration and the service is not monetized through
advertising, affiliate or referral revenue, paid sponsor or promotional
placement, revenue sharing, commercial traffic monetization, paid membership,
paid quota, paid priority, purchased credits, points or tokens, a required
purchase, or another Commercial Hosted Service arrangement. The service must
provide reasonably discoverable attribution to Vanylith, a link to the
original project, and a link to the Vanylith Community Source License 1.0.

9.2. Modified Free Hosted Services. If a Hosted Service uses a Modified
Version, the service must also provide, from a clear and reasonably discoverable
source/license location, free access to the Corresponding Source for the
version actually used by the service. The Corresponding Source must be
available no later than the modified functionality and for as long as that
functionality is offered, and the Vanylith portions and modifications must
remain under this License.

9.3. Commercial Hosted Services Prohibited. Unless the Licensor gives separate
written permission, You may not provide a Commercial Hosted Service using the
Software, a Modified Version, or the core vanity-address-generation
functionality implemented by or derived from the Software. This prohibition
applies even if a customer never receives a copy of the Software. It includes
paid websites, SaaS, APIs, Telegram or Discord bots, remote GPU generation,
managed generation, generation-for-hire, charging by result or address,
subscriptions, purchased quota, credits, points or tokens, and charging by
compute time, GPU hour, attempt, or difficulty. It also includes an otherwise
free-to-use Hosted Service monetized through advertising, affiliate or referral
revenue, paid sponsor or promotional placement, revenue sharing, or commercial
monetization of service traffic.

10. Donations and Sponsorship

You may accept Donations and general project sponsorship that are voluntary,
unconditional, and unrelated to Hosted Service traffic or promotion. A payment
is not a Donation if it is required for, or provides preferential or exclusive
access to, the Software, a Modified Version, source code, a binary, download,
update, feature, generation result, priority, quota, hosted-generation
entitlement, or special build, or if it purchases advertising, sponsor or
promotional placement, referrals, traffic, revenue sharing, or another
commercial benefit connected to a Hosted Service. A sponsor-only release,
member-only download, paid CUDA build, or paid placement on a Hosted Service is
Commercial Distribution or a Commercial Hosted Service, not a Donation. A
neutral acknowledgement of unconditional support in general project materials
is permitted and is not paid Hosted Service placement merely because the
supporter is named.

11. Generated Output

Ordinary output generated through normal use of the Software, including vanity
addresses, benchmark output, locally generated telemetry, and other normal
application output, is not treated as Software or a Modified Version merely
because the Software generated it. This License does not claim ownership of a
Recipient's wallet address, private key, or other generated result.

This section does not authorize a Commercial Hosted Service or generation-for-
hire prohibited by Section 9.3.

12. Corresponding Source and Notice Availability

Where this License requires Corresponding Source or notices, they must be
complete, freely accessible, and obtainable without payment, membership, a
paid account, purchase, or private transaction. The source must correspond to
the binary, package, or hosted version being offered; a promise of later source
availability is insufficient. For a Modified Version that has been externally
distributed, the Corresponding Source must be publicly available to the general
public for the period required by Section 6(b), including at least three (3)
years after the last Distribution of that version when that period ends later.

